{"created": "2020-09-08T12:21:55.500800+00:00", "modified": "2024-07-19T18:18:33.115863+00:00", "id": 3939050, "conceptrecid": "3939049", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3939050", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.3939049", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3939050", "metadata": {"title": "Copernicus Global Land Service: Land Cover 100m: collection 3: epoch 2019: Globe", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3939050", "publication_date": "2020-09-08", "description": "<p>Near real time epoch 2019 from the Collection 3 of annual, global 100m land cover maps.</p>\n\n<p>Other available epochs: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3939038\">2015</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3518026\">2016</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3518036\">2017</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3518038\">2018</a></p>\n\n<p>Produced by the global component of the Copernicus Land Service, derived from PROBA-V satellite observations and ancillary datasets.</p>\n\n<p>The maps include</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>a main discrete classification with 23 classes&nbsp;aligned with UN-FAO&#39;s Land Cover Classification System,</li>\n\t<li>a set of versatile cover fractions: percentage (%) of ground cover for the 10 main classes</li>\n\t<li>a forest type layer</li>\n\t<li>quality layers on input data density and on the confidence of the detected land cover change</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://land.copernicus.eu/global/lcviewer\">Click here to view the maps</a></p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://land.copernicus.eu/global/lcviewer\">More information about the land cover maps</a></p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3606295\">Product User Manual</a></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Marcel Buchhorn", "affiliation": "VITO NV", "orcid": "0000-0002-7922-2161"}, {"name": "Bruno Smets", "affiliation": "VITO NV", "orcid": "0000-0002-3558-8006"}, {"name": "Luc Bertels", "affiliation": "VITO NV", "orcid": "0000-0001-5867-2254"}, {"name": "